---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import CtaPair from "../components/CtaPair.astro";
import FinalCta from "../components/FinalCta.astro";
import PageHero from "../components/PageHero.astro";

const title = "How Launchline Sets Up Your AI | Launchline Design";
const description =
  "From a free 2-minute Loom to a live system in as little as 7 days. You approve every script. A free 14-day Starter pilot is available.";
---

<Base title={title} description={description}>
  <PageHero
    eyebrow="Setup"
    title="Live in as little as 7 days. You approve every script."
    lede="Discovery call, a build around the tools you already use, a test on your real calls, then launch and a monthly tune. The front door is a free Loom on your website."
    crumbs={[
      { href: "/", label: "Home" },
      { href: "/how-it-works", label: "How it works" },
    ]}
  >
    <CtaPair loomHref="/demo#custom-demo" />
  </PageHero>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="wrap">
      <ol class="steps four">
        <li class="step">
          <span class="step-num">1</span>
          <div>
            <h3>Free demo</h3>
            <p>Send your site. We record a 2-minute Loom of how AI would handle your calls and leads. That is the personalized demo, before any package.</p>
          </div>
        </li>
        <li class="step">
          <span class="step-num">2</span>
          <div>
            <h3>Discovery call</h3>
            <p>Fifteen minutes with Myles. We pick a package and map your calls: who answers today, what is urgent, and what the AI must never say.</p>
          </div>
        </li>
        <li class="step">
          <span class="step-num">3</span>
          <div>
            <h3>Build, then test on your real calls</h3>
            <p>Scripts in your voice, connected to your calendar. You hear it before customers do. Starter can run as a free 14-day pilot on your line.</p>
          </div>
        </li>
        <li class="step">
          <span class="step-num">4</span>
          <div>
            <h3>Launch and tune monthly</h3>
            <p>Many Starter and Growth setups go live in as little as 7 days. After that, a monthly check-in. Growth adds call summaries and script optimization.</p>
          </div>
        </li>
      </ol>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section" style="padding-top: 0">
    <div class="wrap two-col">
      <article class="panel">
        <h2>What we need from you</h2>
        <ul class="plain-list" style="margin-top: 0.8rem">
          <li>The business line the AI should watch or answer</li>
          <li>The calendar appointments should land on</li>
          <li>Who gets an urgent alert, and how</li>
          <li>Services, hours, and any prices the AI is allowed to say</li>
          <li>The list of things it must hand to a person</li>
        </ul>
      </article>
      <article class="pilot">
        <p class="slot-kicker">Free 14-day Starter pilot</p>
        <h2>Keep it only if it is catching calls.</h2>
        <p style="margin-top: 0.6rem">
          We set up Starter on your line at no cost. If it is not catching calls you would have missed, you do not keep it. The pilot is Starter: text-back, review requests, and the shared inbox. The voice receptionist is Growth.
        </p>
      </article>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section" style="padding-top: 0">
    <div class="wrap prose">
      <h2>What “as little as 7 days” does and does not mean</h2>
      <p>
        It is a real timeline for many Starter and Growth setups once the script is approved and the calendar access is in place. It is not a promise for every scope. Custom AI is quoted in a written proposal, and that proposal carries the timeline.
      </p>
      <p>
        Phone, SMS, and AI usage are billed at cost with no markup. Your accounts, numbers, and data stay yours. Questions on recording consent, HIPAA scope, and handoff are on the <a href="/#faq">homepage FAQ</a>.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
  <FinalCta />
</Base>
